Support identities and composition for morphisms

Allow rules to express identity maps and chains of model morphisms using
id(model) and first >> second, with member access binding more tightly.
Infer model types and endpoints in either direction and preserve nested
member typing when identities or composites supply parent images.

Reuse existing morphisms for unit and associativity laws so closure does
not enumerate a free category. Propagate identity and composite actions
through known member images. Rename example identity functions to keep
id available as a builtin. Expose identity and composition roles in
runtime signatures so dynamic clients can distinguish generated
operations.

Cover valid evaluation, partial actions, nested members, composition
order, associativity, and invalid operands with integration tests.
